      "id": "andlauer-julien",
      "wikidata": "Q99264546",
      "summary": {
        "text": "Julien Andlauer (born 5 July 1999 in Lyon) is a French racing driver. He is a Porsche factory driver, and competes in the IMSA SportsCar Championship for Porsche Penske Motorsport.\n\nA dual Porsche Carrera Cup champion in his youth, Andlauer developed into one of the leading LMGTE Am drivers, and was a 24 Hours of Le Mans class winner on debut in 2018. He made his LMDh debut for Proton in 2024, and notably took the lead of the 6 Hours of Spa with four overtakes at Eau Rouge. Andlauer was promoted to the Porsche factory team in 2025, and won the 24 Hours of Daytona and 12 Hours of Sebring overall in 2026.",
        "lang": "en",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julien_Andlauer"
      },
